sops.workflow:
1. User -> Transportation Planner;
2. Transportation Planner -> Accommodation Planner (only if transportation plan validates city continuity and sandbox data);
3. Accommodation Planner -> Restaurant Planner and Accommodation Planner -> Attractions Planner (in parallel; only if minimum-stay compliance is confirmed);
4. Restaurant Planner, Attractions Planner -> Final Plan Summarizer (only if city-day meal/attraction mappings align);
5. Final Plan Summarizer -> End (if all critical validations pass).

Description:
Transportation Planner first constructs a complete day-by-day itinerary for ALL calendar days (March 6-10) with explicit 'from [X] to [Y]' segments, validating Day 1 departs from Santa Ana and all flight numbers against sandbox data. Accommodation Planner then verifies minimum-stay compliance against consecutive-night counts per city and halts on violations. Restaurant and Attractions Planners work in parallel using parsed city contexts (departure city for pre-transit meals, arrival city for post-transit meals/attractions). Final Plan Summarizer performs strict validation in priority order: (1) city continuity and alignment, (2) transportation data sandbox validity, (3) budget constraints. Any inconsistency triggers immediate halt with specific error.
